  "answer": "### Short Answer\nAn individual has until April 15 of the following year to file their annual income tax return.\n\n### Interpretation\nThe deadline for filing the annual income tax return is set to ensure that individuals report their income and pay any taxes due in a timely manner. The April 15 deadline allows the Bureau of Internal Revenue (BIR) to process returns and collect taxes efficiently.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nTaxpayers should prepare their financial records and tax documents well in advance of the April 15 deadline to avoid penalties for late filing. It is advisable to consult with a tax professional if there are complexities in the income or deductions to ensure compliance with tax laws.",
